<%--
_Apidocs_File_Endpoint_Card - the endpoint card for a multipart/form-data endpoint.

SLOTS ONLY, so the whole card - verb pills, description, parameters, example response, the
two-column split - is inherited from _Apidocs_Endpoint_Card and exists in exactly one file. The
one thing a file endpoint genuinely needs differently is the tester: a JSON textarea cannot
carry a binary part, and posting a filename as text would only ever earn a 422.

The code samples need NO override: api_code_samples() reads the endpoint spec and dispatches
to the multipart generator on its own, so the samples cannot disagree with the transport.
--%>
<Define:_Apidocs_File_Endpoint_Card extends="_Apidocs_Endpoint_Card" tag="article">
    <Slot:tester>
        <_Apidocs_File_Tester $endpoint=this.args.endpoint />
    </Slot:tester>
</Define:_Apidocs_File_Endpoint_Card>
